# QA check plan, round 1 (against producer `brief.md`)

Each candidate gets a report `qa/reports/<build>.md`: every ID below as PASS / FAIL / BLOCKED / NOT-BUILT, with the method (A = automated headless Chromium via `qa/smoke.py` or ad-hoc Playwright scripts with key input + screenshots; M = manual frame-by-frame inspection of screenshots/state). Defects go as issues to the owner (`game-developer` behaviour/code, `artist` assets), with build tag, steps, expected vs actual, evidence.

## G. General (brief "Standard")
- G1 Opens from static `index.html` (file:// and static server), no console errors, no network requests off-origin (runs offline).
- G2 Canvas is 256x240 logical, integer-scaled, pixel-crisp (no smoothing), 16x16 tiles.
- G3 Logic at 60 fps, speed independent of display refresh; no softlocks, no falling through floors, no stuck in walls.
- G4 Controls: arrows, Down crouch/pipe, Z/J = B, X/K/Space = A, Enter start/pause; documented on title or README; no stuck keys after blur.
- G5 Assets original recreations (no ripped ROM/Nintendo audio): check asset provenance notes.
## P1. World 1-1
- L1 Layout vs original: ground gaps, ?/brick placement, pipes (heights 2,3,4,4), stairs, flagpole, castle; level length ~212 tiles.
- L2 Hidden 1-up block, multi-coin brick, Starman brick, enterable pipe to underground coin room and exit pipe back.
- M1 Walk/run with acceleration and skid; M2 variable jump height (hold time, run speed); M3 air control; M4 camera scrolls forward only, left screen edge blocks Mario.
- E1 Goomba walks, turns at walls, stomp flatten +100, bounce; E2 Koopa: stomp -> shell, kick, shell kills enemies and hurts Mario; E3 enemies fall into pits; E4 touch hurts Mario; E5 enemies activate on approach.
- P1 Super Mushroom (small->big, appears from first ?, moves, falls); P2 big breaks bricks, small bumps; P3 Fire Flower + fireballs bounce and kill; P4 Starman invincibility; P5 1-up mushroom; P6 damage: big->small with invulnerability blink, small dies.
- C1 Coins from blocks and floating coins, +score; C2 100 coins = 1-up.
- H1 HUD: MARIO score, coins, WORLD 1-1, TIME 400 countdown; H2 time-out kills; H3 hurry-up at 100.
- D1 Lives start 3; D2 death animation, respawn; D3 pit death; D4 game over screen -> title/restart; D5 title screen with start.
- F1 Flagpole: height-based score, slide, walk to castle, time converted to score, course clear; F2 completable start-to-flag by script.
- S1 SFX: jump, coin, stomp, bump, break, power-up appear/get, 1-up, pipe, fireball, death, flagpole, course clear, game over; S2 music overworld, underground, hurry-up; S3 audio starts after first input (autoplay policy), no errors.
## P2. Rest of World 1 (only if built)
- 1-2 underground + warp zone, Piranha Plants; 1-3 treetops + lifts; 1-4 firebars, lava, Bowser, axe, Toad; transitions between levels.
## Edge cases to hit on every build
Pause during death/flag; hold both directions; jump at ceiling gap; stomp two enemies in a row (combo score); shell kicked into Mario; pipe entry with partial overlap; resize window; tab blur/focus; restart after game over without reload.
